{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COMSTACK_SECTION_7_3_5_Flow_Control_FC","src":"manifest","doc":"SWS_FlexRayARTransportLayer","page":35,"text":"7.3.5 Flow Control (FC)\n[SWS_FrArTp_00064] ⌈A Flow Control frame is used in segmented 1:1 connections.\nThus, it cannot appear in a 1:n connection. It allows the receiver to send information\nto the sender. It is sent after reception of an FF-x and after the last CF of a block if no\nerror occurred.⌋\nFlow Control Frames consist of FT, FS, BS, and STmin fields as depicted in the Table","caption":"7.3.5 Flow Control (FC)","sha":null,"series":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COMSTACK_SECTION_7_3_5_Flow_Control_FC","releases":["R23-11"],"page":37,"hash":"f37c6f4c1b1b8b90","caption":""},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COMSTACK_SECTION_7_3_5_Flow_Control_FC","releases":["R24-11"],"page":36,"hash":"9364ce0ad37e9bef","caption":""},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COMSTACK_SECTION_7_3_5_Flow_Control_FC","releases":["R25-11"],"page":35,"hash":"de96d86efdeb8f4f","caption":""}],"releases":["R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"kind":"snippet","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_FrArTp_00064] im Text von SWS_FlexRayARTransportLayer.","rel":["R25-11"],"id":"SWS_FrArTp_00064"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Flow Control frame layout definition","rel":[],"id":"SWS_FrArTp_00240"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.75,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"FrArTp FC frame handling behavior","rel":[],"id":"SWS_FrArTp_00283"}],"ok":true,"schema":"versions-explorer@1"}